// Mission -
//  A mission, as cortext's mission registry stores it: one governed object per
//  mission, homed in the `.models` system directory beside `ModelManifest` and
//  `OntologyDeclaration` (the same governed-object recipe), with an ACL the
//  owner controls and the platform's own revision history.
//
//  The object is a *reference*, like the other two: the mission document is a
//  Drive file named here by id, content revision and sha256, and the fields a
//  reader queries on (city, status, objectives, KPIs, variants, bindings) are
//  projected once per source revision into the `missions` registry
//  (registry.fbs), so nothing on a read path opens the document. The document
//  is JSON — it is cortext's own rendering of the mission, not an authored
//  file — while `spec` names the `mission.yaml` a person dropped, kept as
//  provenance the way an ontology keeps its bronze file.
//
//  The mission document holds only asserted state. What a mission has *done*
//  (its messages, decisions, runs and the activity line derived from them) is
//  not here and does not revise the object: a revision is a change to what the
//  mission *is*, which is what makes the chain readable as a history of
//  decisions rather than of chatter.
